@*
    DesktopRedirectToLogin.razor
    Purpose: The desktop head's replacement for the shared RedirectToLogin (REQ-UI-051).

    The shared component force-reloads the document (forceLoad: true) and carries a returnUrl. Both
    are right for a website and wrong for BlogApp:
      * a BlazorWebView has no address bar and cannot rely on a document reload - reloading while a
        menu's JavaScript references are still alive (a logout from the account menu) left the window
        on "An unhandled error has occurred" until the operator reloaded it by hand;
      * there are no deep links to return to, and a guessed returnUrl sends an Author who signs in
        after an Admin to /admin and on to access-denied (see DesktopStart).
    So this one navigates inside the running app, replaces the history entry, and lets the sign-in
    screen choose the role's landing route.
*@
@inject NavigationManager NavigationManager

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// Moves to the sign-in screen without reloading the document.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <para><b>Flow:</b> initialise → navigate to <c>/login</c>, replacing the current entry.</para>
    /// <para><b>Side Effects:</b> Changes the route.</para>
    /// </remarks>
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        NavigationManager.NavigateTo("/login", replace: true);
    }
}
